✈️ This script will help you migrate to a LangChain 0.3. This migration script 
will attempt to replace old imports in the code with new ones. If you need to 
migrate to LangChain 0.2, please downgrade to version 0.0.29 of the 
langchain-cli.

🔄 You will need to run the migration script TWICE to migrate (e.g., to update 
llms import from langchain, the script will first move them to corresponding 
imports from the community package, and on the second run will migrate from the 
community package to the partner package when possible). 

🔍 You can pre-view the changes by running with the --diff flag. 

🚫 You can disable specific import changes by using the --disable flag. 

📄 Update your pyproject.toml or requirements.txt file to reflect any imports 
from new packages. For example, if you see new imports from langchain_openai, 
langchain_anthropic or langchain_text_splitters you should add them to your 
dependencies! 

⚠️ This script is a "best-effort", and is likely to make some mistakes.

🛡️ Backup your code prior to running the migration script -- it will modify your
files!


